ions and  opinions seem to be well spread across  the whole kaleidoscope there's many  people who have uh a massive amount of  of sympathy uh for jennifer roberts and  and her status as a victim  there's also a lot of uh  sympathy for the queen in all of this  you know prince andrew was said to be  her favorite son and his fall from grace  uh has no doubt pained the royal family  and the queen in particular and so  there's a lot of public sympathy for the  queen in all of this and the other  overriding sentiment is that look if  prince andrew who has denied any uh  impropriety if he really has nothing to  hide then he should cooperate with  prosecutors and and with this case  that's the other third strand of public  opinion that i'm detecting as a distinct  sort of trail  it's going to be fascinating to see how  it turns out thank you for that update  paul brennan live for us in london
 

